- 2026-07-26: `gllm/layers/quantization/awq.py` (new file, GreenBoost
  addition) — AWQ (4-bit only, `zero_point: true` only) weight registration
  and forward dequant+matmul, reusing GPTQ's already-vendored
  `gptqmodel.nn_modules.triton_utils.dequant.quant_matmul` Triton kernel
  rather than adding a second one: AWQ and GPTQ checkpoints store the
  identical logical `[in_features, out_features]` matrix, group-quantized
  the same way, so once AWQ's two real format differences are corrected the
  GPTQ kernel dequants an AWQ checkpoint correctly. The two differences
  (checked against AutoAWQ's own layout and vLLM's `auto_awq.py` reference
  conversion), both fixed once, lazily, on first forward pass in
  `_maybe_convert_awq_layout()` (the real packed values only exist after
  the weight loader has filled them):
    1. Packing axis — AWQ packs `qweight` along the OUTPUT dim
       (`[in_features, out_features // pack_factor]`); GPTQ's kernel expects
       it packed along the INPUT dim
       (`[in_features // pack_factor, out_features]`). `qzeros` already
       matches GPTQ's axis convention on disk, no change needed there.
    2. Bit order within a packed word — AWQ interleaves sub-values as
       `[0,4,1,5,2,6,3,7]` (4-bit); GPTQ uses plain sequential order.
       `_AWQ_PACK_ORDER`/the unpack-reorder-repack math is copied from
       vLLM's `auto_awq.py` (`_REVERSE_AWQ_PACK_ORDER`), a previously
       solved/tested constant, not re-derived.
  No g_idx checkpoint key (AWQ has no `desc_act` equivalent): a trivial
  `arange(in_features) // group_size` is computed once and kept as a plain
  unregistered tensor attribute (never a checkpoint-loaded Parameter), so
  the weight loader never looks for a `.g_idx` key no AWQ checkpoint has on
  disk. No v1/v2 zero-point offset quirk either (GPTQ-specific) — AWQ's raw
  `qzeros` already encode the true zero point directly.

