  torch.arange/"invalid resource handle", ones_/"invalid resource handle",
  torch.rand/SIGFPE — happen on CPU); `.to("cuda")` is a plain per-tensor
  device copy, a different code path already confirmed safe in isolation.
  Verified end-to-end with a standalone repro (nested device-context +
  Conv3d + torch.rand + bulk `.to("cuda")`, shim active) before deploying.
  `_skip_random_init()` itself is kept (skipping useless CPU random-init is
  a free speed optimization even without the crash to avoid — no downside
  to leaving it).

